1 FOREIGN

   A foreign command runs an image with the rest of the command line as
   its command text, which the image reads with LIB$GET_FOREIGN.  Define
   one with a symbol whose value is "$" and the image's file name (see
   Symbol_Assign):

     $ FORTH :== $DUA1:[TOOLS]FORTH.EXE
     $ FORTH 2 3 + . CR

   The image is found as RUN finds it.  The command text is treated as
   DCL treats a command's parameters: outside quotes it is made
   uppercase and its blanks are compressed, and a "!" begins a comment;
   quoted text, quotes and all, is passed as typed.  MCR runs an image
   the same way without a symbol.
